<title>JAPAN: Japan cooperating with G7 on forex -- MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan cooperating with G7 on forex -- MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka told Reuters on Friday that Japan is cooperating with Group of Seven (G7) nations on currencies and will continue to do so.  </p>
<p>Asked whether the United States shared Japan's stance on foreign exchange, he said: &quot;We are cooperating with G7 nations and we will continue to do so.&quot;</p>
<p>Japan has said excessive weakness in the yen and excessive strength in the yen are undesirable.</p>
</text>
